+# Strain-preserving geometric bias — optional bounded prototype
+
+The optional `preserve-strain` variant removes the elastic deformation introduced by the compliant bias on the tilted stress-free plane witness. It also passes the unchanged eight native World oracles. The translated-mouth case still fails final physical contact closure. The default bias option remains `physical-compliance`.
+
+Enable per joint, between timesteps:
+
+```js
+import { configureKirchhoffSplitBias } from './src/physics/kirchhoffSplitMotion.js';
+configureKirchhoffSplitBias(joint, { materialMode: 'preserve-strain' });
+```
+
+Only CoupledSystem and SplitMotion production sources change. World, physical EI/GJ/compliance, rest data, tolerances, damping, force gradients, inverse-mass metric and solver backend are untouched.
+
+## Equations
+
+The physical phase is identical in both variants. It solves the native material equations and captures `C_phys` before geometric bias. The existing compliant bias solves
+
+`(C_geo - C_phys) + alpha_physical * lambda_bias = 0`.
+
+The optional variant instead solves
+
+`C_geo - C_phys = 0`, with `alpha_bias = 0`.
+
+Thus each coupled material bias row has RHS `-(C_geo-C_phys)` and zero diagonal compliance. This changes neither the native material assembly nor the physical multiplier bank. The bias convergence measurement uses exactly the same hard strain difference. After restoring physical multipliers, the final material gate still evaluates fresh `C_geo + alpha_physical * lambda_physical`; the old phase residual is never substituted for it. No new Newton loop or outer reclosure was introduced.
+
+## Tilted stress-free plane witness
+
+Three wire nodes initially have x=`[-1,0,1]`, y=`[-.7,-.5,-.3]`, radius .5, captured straight rest shape, zero physical input. An independent fixed five-node rod supplies the JOINT pair. Plane lumen is y<=0. Bend/twist compliance .02, adaptation compliance 0. Both variants perform actual World physical and bias solves.
+
+| Final quantity | Existing compliant bias | Preserve strain |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| Raw minimum plane gap, mm | 0 | 0 |
+| Maximum native strain drift from physical phase | .07894805165337379 | 1.0208563883118416e-7 |
+| Fresh bend/twist residual, rad | .07894805165337379 | 1.7496861847463106e-24 |
+| Fresh adaptation residual, mm | 2.386899020579232e-7 | 1.2051144559080793e-7 |
+| Bias elastic energy change | .1558198714965944 | 0 |
+| Sum physical Fn / Ft (XPBD multipliers) | 0 / 0 | 0 / 0 |
+| Final certified / history commits | false / 0 | true / 1 |
+
+Physical v and omega arrays are bit-for-bit equal between variants. Both retain the tiny physical correction already caused by the Float32-captured rest length: maximum |v|=2.2045965124561917e-6 mm/s and maximum |omega| about 6.244e-16 rad/s. These are far below the unchanged independent oracle bounds; bias adds no physical motion. Native physical alpha arrays have zero before/after difference; all rest and EI/GJ compliance arrays are unchanged.
+
+The new test also checks adjacent quaternions independently (no relative bend/twist), geometric segment lengths, raw plane gaps and physical reaction banks. A fully immobile penetrating wire is intentionally infeasible and remains `biasAccepted=false`, `certified=false`, `historyCommits=0`; no gate was weakened to accept it.
+
+Raw comparison JSON: `/tmp/oet-split-preserve-strain-first-8996.json`, generated by `reports/probe-split-preserve-strain.mjs`.
+
+## Unchanged eight World oracles
+
+The external 0827 file was not edited. A test-only Node preload wraps `addContainment` to call the per-joint option setter for an already selected split World; it does not change any fixture input, assertion, tolerance or solver result.
+
+- Existing bias: **8 PASS / 0 FAIL**, `/tmp/oet-preserve-strain-reference-oracle-8996.txt`.
+- Preserve strain: **8 PASS / 0 FAIL**, `/tmp/oet-split-preserve-strain-oracle-8996.txt`.
+- New behavior tests: **2 PASS / 0 FAIL**, `tests/kirchhoffSplitBiasStrain.test.js`.
+- CoupledSystem plus existing split certification tests, default options: **21 PASS / 0 FAIL**, `/tmp/oet-preserve-strain-default-8996.txt`.
+
+Example option run:
+
+```sh
+OET_SPLIT_MOTION_SOURCE_ROOT=/Users/macpiek/.codex/worktrees/8996/OpenEndovascularTrainer node --import ./reports/register-split-preserve-strain.mjs --test --test-concurrency=1 /Users/macpiek/.codex/worktrees/0827/OpenEndovascularTrainer/tests/kirchhoffSplitMotionWorld.test.js
+```
+
+## Translated-mouth comparison
+
+Exactly one extra execution of the existing `probe-translated-split-world.mjs` used the same preload. The probe, its controls and its witnesses were not edited. No anatomy or outer reclosure ran.
+
+| Final quantity | Existing compliant bias | Preserve strain |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| Bias elastic energy change | 1.2561989880728693e-6 | 0 |
+| Fresh bend/twist residual, rad | 5.01238264317136e-5 | 2.214997901917172e-16 |
+| Fresh adaptation residual, mm | 4.768384160547769e-7 | 4.770205541233562e-7 |
+| Physical KKT displacement residual, mm | .0016996188682287892 | .0016996190233046005 |
+| Maximum outward contact velocity, mm/s | .20395426418745471 | .20395428279655206 |
+| Physical Fn / Ft | 0 / 0 | 0 / 0 |
+| Final certified / history commits | false / 0 | false / 0 |
+
+Each variant accepts its one physical and one bias phase, then fails the fresh final physical contact gate. Removing bias elastic deformation does not close the new physical contact: the residual differs by only 1.55e-10 mm. Further physical reclosure and root's failed-step transaction remain separate work. Logs are `/tmp/oet-translated-split-final-8996.txt` and `/tmp/oet-translated-preserve-strain-8996.txt`.
+
+This checkpoint establishes the bounded hypothesis on these fixtures. General feasibility with many fixed supports, nonlinear contacts and runtime anatomy is not claimed. Existing wall material-foot ownership, migration, CCD and final-failure handling limitations from the prior handoff remain open.
